rd Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 70 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mike Lawler (R) is running."]}, "overview": "New York's 17th District is a narrowly Democratic-leaning swing seat where Republican incumbent Mike Lawler faces Democrat Cait Conley. Lawler has proven competitive here before and has raised far more money, with a large cash-on-hand advantage. Conley has still posted strong fundraising and drawn substantial outside support and opposition spending.\n\nMost expert raters call the race a Tossup, though several lean toward a Democratic flip, and prediction markets give Conley roughly a 60-65% chance. The available polls are few, dated, and sponsored by partisan groups, so they add little clarity. The race sits as a genuine tossup with a slight Democratic tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7399, "margin": 4.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7185, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6936, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7094, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6393, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6716, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7011, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7074, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6916, "margin": 3.0}]}